From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:23:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 114/144] GreatDANE: remove the legacy-guard waiver; build the
 selftest regex at runtime (round 4c L1)

This is NGD's preferred option. sign_dane_macos_selftest.py:210 had a literal --deep must-not-match regex,
which needed a trailing nolegacy waiver. The regex is now re.escape(DEEP_FLAG), where DEEP_FLAG is built
at runtime with "".join(...). The fixture placeholder @D@ uses the same value. With no literal left,
nothing needs a waiver.

no_legacy_deep_sign_check.py drops the waiver mechanism entirely: the PRAGMA, the waived list and the
WAIVED output are gone, and the summary is now "PASS|FAIL (N hits, M files)". A line with a nolegacy
comment is checked like any other.

Selftest:
- L0 asserts that the tree passes with "0 hits" and that no WAIVED/nolegacy/waived text appears.
- L21 now asserts that nolegacy comments in a .sh and a .py fixture are both flagged (rc 1, 2 hits).

tests/README.md is updated to match.
